      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "SOHO WASHINGTON (4) drew poorly and had to work in a heat of this series last start so wasn't disgraced when midfield behind subsequent final winner Enjoy Life. Scored a hat trick of wins earlier in the campaign, leading each time so he has the pace to take advantage of the better draw. BINALONG MATE (1) kicked off his campaign with a win at this venue and has placed in two of three starts since, the miss coming from a tough draw in the heats. Should get his chance from the inside barrier. ZANDA MAN (5) is two from two when third up so should be peaking and he owns good statistics both here and at the distance so must be respected. KING BALDWIN (3) takes a step up in grade but looked good when coming from wider for an easy debut win at Cranbourne and is open to improvement.",
